course: dictionary
lesson: 12426
title: Words that are very loud
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture of a sound. «Thunder crashed overhead, a deafening boom that made the windows shake.» The clues are the boom and the shaking windows. Deafening means so loud you can hardly hear anything else.
explain: Deafening is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a deafening noise, a deafening roar, deafening applause. Look for the word it describes to find what is so loud. «The music got more deafening as the band played on.» Here the music is the thing that gets louder.
explain: Sometimes deafening describes silence, which sounds odd at first. «The class sat in deafening silence when the teacher asked who had broken the window.» Nobody answered, and the silence was so noticeable that it felt loud. Writers use this idiom to show that a silence means something.
fact: Deafening means extremely loud, so loud you can hardly hear anything else.
fact: «A deafening roar» is a very loud roar, and «deafening applause» is clapping so loud it fills the whole hall.
fact: «A deafening silence» is an idiom: a silence that people notice strongly, for example when someone refuses to answer.
fact: In stories, deafening noises such as thunder, cheering crowds or explosions tell the reader that the sound is overwhelming.
fact: Very loud sounds can damage your hearing, so use ear defenders near loud machines or at noisy events.
exercise: «The thunder gave a deafening crash.» What does deafening mean here? | Gentle and soft | Bright and shiny | *Extremely loud | Very quiet
exercise: «The crowd gave deafening applause.» Find and copy the one word that tells you the applause was very loud. | crowd | applause | gave | *deafening
exercise: Tom says «deafening silence» means there is no sound at all. What is the best answer? | It means the crowd is cheering | It means a noise so loud that you go deaf for ever | It means a silence with no sound, exactly the same as quiet | *It is an idiom: a silence so noticeable it feels loud, such as when people refuse to answer
test: «The music was so deafening that we covered our ears.» What does deafening mean? | Bright and colourful | *Extremely loud | Very slow | Very quiet
test: Why might a sign tell you to wear ear defenders near a loud machine? | Because sunlight can hurt your eyes | *Because very loud sounds can damage your hearing | Because noise is always fun | Because they keep your hands warm
exam: «After the teacher asked a question, the class stayed in deafening silence.» What does this mean? | Everyone had fallen asleep | The class was singing a loud song | *Nobody spoke, and the silence was very noticeable | Everyone was shouting at once
